WEBVTT

00:43.001 --> 00:43.877
Did you also

00:45.045 --> 00:46.046
know about it?

00:46.713 --> 00:48.923
Sir, what's this about?

00:49.007 --> 00:50.300
Did you know

00:51.968 --> 00:54.220
that Nu-a was also
taking part in this project?

00:55.221 --> 00:56.055
Ms. Kook?

00:59.976 --> 01:01.644
What do you mean?

01:04.856 --> 01:08.401
Sir. We can talk about that later.

01:09.360 --> 01:10.278
See?

01:11.946 --> 01:13.448
You're always the one…

01:15.408 --> 01:16.576
who ruins me.

01:26.252 --> 01:29.547
It all started…

01:30.882 --> 01:31.716
YEAR 2000

01:31.800 --> 01:33.510
- …a long time ago.
- It's you, right?

01:33.593 --> 01:35.970
- You're here!
- Your dad runs Ung's Snack Bar, right?

01:36.054 --> 01:39.140
You're so lucky.
Do you eat free tteokbokki every day?

01:39.224 --> 01:41.434
- Can I come?
- Me too!

01:41.518 --> 01:43.186
It was all because of our names.

01:43.269 --> 01:44.729
- You got the wrong person.
- What?

01:44.813 --> 01:46.648
My dad doesn't run the snack bar.

01:47.941 --> 01:48.983
His dad does.

01:51.903 --> 01:53.363
"Kim Ji-ung?"

01:53.446 --> 01:55.532
So your dad runs Ung's Snack Bar?

01:55.615 --> 01:57.117
It must be him!

01:57.200 --> 01:59.661
Hey, let's be friends.

01:59.744 --> 02:02.038
- Come on.
- Hey, Choi Ung!

02:02.122 --> 02:04.999
It was like The Prince and the Pauper…

02:05.083 --> 02:06.626
- Come on.
- I want to go.

02:06.709 --> 02:07.544
GAMJATANG WITH UNG

02:07.627 --> 02:09.963
…where the prince and the pauper
had similar names.

02:10.964 --> 02:12.590
- Thanks for the food.
- Sure.

02:15.468 --> 02:16.594
- To be honest…
- Goodness.

02:16.678 --> 02:18.888
- …why would a kid be jealous of that?
- You must be Ung. Gosh.

02:18.972 --> 02:22.392
You're lucky to have
a restaurant named after you.

02:22.475 --> 02:23.977
That's right.

02:24.686 --> 02:26.896
Are you going to take on
the family business?

02:26.980 --> 02:29.983
Of course he will.
The restaurant was named after him.

02:30.066 --> 02:30.942
To a kid…

02:31.025 --> 02:33.278
- You're so lucky.
- …it sounded like nonsense.

02:38.324 --> 02:39.617
Hey.

02:39.701 --> 02:42.453
Don't you dare lie like that again.

02:44.289 --> 02:45.790
Oh, I'm sorry.

02:47.208 --> 02:49.669
- What are you doing here?
- I'm just sitting here.

02:49.752 --> 02:52.255
How come you've been
sitting here for hours?

02:53.047 --> 02:55.675
Mom told me to stay put and play here.

02:55.758 --> 02:56.634
Why?

02:57.677 --> 02:59.012
She said it's dangerous.

02:59.971 --> 03:02.098
And he seemed a bit pathetic

03:03.099 --> 03:05.101
to be a prince.

03:06.311 --> 03:07.520
Funny, right?

03:08.271 --> 03:09.856
Me feeling sorry for someone.

03:37.216 --> 03:38.843
I guess he seemed more lonely…

03:44.557 --> 03:45.892
than pathetic.

03:50.355 --> 03:53.858
WITH UNG

03:58.613 --> 04:00.406
Do you want to hear a scary story?

04:04.118 --> 04:07.830
I'm not making this up.
It really happened.

04:08.706 --> 04:11.876
Every night at 12 a.m.,
when the bell rang three times…

04:13.753 --> 04:15.672
I think that's how we became friends.

04:18.591 --> 04:23.429
But having a friend
didn't make much of a difference.

04:27.517 --> 04:30.728
- I have to go eat.
- You're leaving to eat again?

04:30.812 --> 04:32.313
What are you, a puppy?

04:33.731 --> 04:36.067
I had fun today. See you tomorrow.

04:40.488 --> 04:43.491
In the end, I was all alone.

04:47.370 --> 04:49.998
Hey, when is your mom coming home?

04:51.249 --> 04:52.375
Late at night.

04:52.959 --> 04:55.461
- How come?
- She's working.

04:56.713 --> 04:57.922
What about your dad?

04:59.299 --> 05:01.009
I don't have a dad.

05:03.052 --> 05:04.971
Then who do you eat with?

05:10.643 --> 05:12.061
Ta-da.

05:12.687 --> 05:14.188
Eat up, Ji-ung.

05:14.272 --> 05:16.899
Thank you, ma'am. Thank you, sir.

05:16.983 --> 05:19.319
Gosh, you're so polite.

05:19.861 --> 05:24.824
Your name is similar to my son's
and you're so polite and smart.

05:24.907 --> 05:28.286
One, two, three. Ta-da.

05:29.829 --> 05:33.374
- It's hot!
- Come and have dinner with us often, okay?

05:33.458 --> 05:35.960
Thank you for being
such good friends with Ung.

05:36.586 --> 05:39.589
What do you want, Ung? Eggs?
Do you want eggs?

05:39.672 --> 05:41.841
Let's see… Here.

05:41.924 --> 05:43.551
- What about you Ji-ung?
- Meat.

05:43.634 --> 05:46.888
- Right. Have some meat. Here.
- Meat.

05:46.971 --> 05:49.223
Okay. What about me?

05:49.307 --> 05:50.767
- You eat on your own.
- Gosh.

05:50.850 --> 05:52.143
- I had never been…
- A sausage.

05:52.226 --> 05:53.728
…that jealous of someone before.

05:54.312 --> 05:55.438
Dig in.

05:55.521 --> 05:58.107
I'll have garlic scapes.

06:00.026 --> 06:02.278
I thought I'll never be able to
have what he has.

06:02.361 --> 06:03.404
Here you go, Ung.

06:03.488 --> 06:05.448
- What?
- Look.

06:05.990 --> 06:07.617
Okay, line up everyone.

06:07.700 --> 06:08.993
- Come forward.
- But…

06:09.077 --> 06:10.536
My seat.

06:11.120 --> 06:13.581
My mom packed sausage gimbap for me.

06:13.664 --> 06:15.083
- Do you want to share?
- Okay.

06:15.166 --> 06:16.793
What's that?

06:20.171 --> 06:21.589
This is for you.

06:23.299 --> 06:24.842
But Choi Ung didn't seem to be jealous.

06:28.137 --> 06:29.138
Are you done eating?

06:29.222 --> 06:30.431
Thank you for the food.

06:30.515 --> 06:32.892
Gosh, you're so polite.

06:33.392 --> 06:34.685
Eat up.

06:34.769 --> 06:36.646
I heard you guys are going bike riding.

06:36.729 --> 06:39.398
Excuse me, ma'am.
Could you come taste this?

06:39.482 --> 06:42.401
Okay. Dig in. Have some bananas too.

06:42.485 --> 06:43.569
Okay.

06:49.242 --> 06:50.368
Can you eat some for me?

06:59.085 --> 07:02.255
Choi Ung shared everything with me
as if he was supposed to.

07:20.565 --> 07:21.691
He shared his time…

07:25.236 --> 07:27.280
Come on. That's cheating.

07:28.322 --> 07:31.075
I told you, you can't beat me.

07:31.617 --> 07:32.994
Sir, let me help you.

07:33.077 --> 07:34.620
It's okay.

07:34.704 --> 07:36.914
It's okay, Ji-ung.

07:36.998 --> 07:39.208
Put it down. It's heavy.

07:39.292 --> 07:42.003
Choi Ung. Where do you think you're going?

07:42.587 --> 07:43.754
Ji-ung is strong.

07:43.838 --> 07:45.798
- Gosh, that little…
- …his daily life…

07:45.882 --> 07:47.091
Then Ji-ung…

07:47.175 --> 07:50.511
Here I go. One, two, three.

07:52.221 --> 07:53.639
Hey, come on over here.

07:53.723 --> 07:55.641
- Yes. Come here, Ji-ung.
- Sir.

07:55.725 --> 07:57.602
Thank you. Come over here, Ji-ung.

07:57.685 --> 08:02.356
Sir, please make sure my two sons
look good in the photo.

08:02.440 --> 08:03.566
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR GRADUATION

08:05.735 --> 08:06.736
…and even his family.

08:06.819 --> 08:08.446
Smile.

08:08.529 --> 08:11.365
- Smile.
- One, two, three.

08:12.200 --> 08:17.330
Thanks to him, I was able to
imitate happiness in my life.

08:24.170 --> 08:28.257
But there's always a third character
in stories like these.

08:43.022 --> 08:45.942
It's obvious. It's so obvious, but…

09:05.211 --> 09:06.754
It seemed like you needed it.

09:16.138 --> 09:16.973
Do you

09:18.307 --> 09:19.308
need this back?

09:20.810 --> 09:22.937
- Of course not.
- Thanks.

09:27.692 --> 09:29.652
She was unbelievably beautiful.

09:32.071 --> 09:34.323
HWIYEONG HIGH SCHOOL ENTRANCE CEREMONY

09:38.035 --> 09:40.246
The principal will now make a speech.

09:46.002 --> 09:48.754
Spring is finally here.

09:48.838 --> 09:51.716
The weather is pretty cold.

09:51.799 --> 09:54.635
I would like to extend my gratitude…

09:59.140 --> 09:59.974
But…

10:01.100 --> 10:03.561
I wasn't the only one who thought so.

10:05.396 --> 10:06.981
That's how the story always goes.

10:07.773 --> 10:11.319
But it wasn't a problem.

10:24.498 --> 10:25.541
All I had to do was…

10:28.085 --> 10:31.005
take a step back.

10:35.926 --> 10:37.428
I don't think

10:38.471 --> 10:41.098
I'm the main character in this life.

10:42.433 --> 10:43.851
Let's wrap it up now.

10:43.934 --> 10:44.977
Thanks.

10:47.146 --> 10:49.565
A SECRET THAT CAN'T BE TOLD

10:49.649 --> 10:53.361
EPISODE 5

10:56.030 --> 10:58.240
Things got
more complicated than I thought.

11:01.035 --> 11:03.537
- Mr. Jang.
- Yes, Ms. Kook?

11:03.621 --> 11:05.998
What did he mean just now?

11:06.082 --> 11:08.542
Will Nu-a be participating in the project?

11:09.168 --> 11:10.127
It's just as he said.

11:10.211 --> 11:13.130
Didn't I send you the data
proving he didn't plagiarize anyone?

11:13.214 --> 11:15.049
- So how could you--
- One second.

11:18.677 --> 11:19.720
Excuse me.

11:24.225 --> 11:26.936
What is the one thing
we need most right now?

11:29.230 --> 11:30.398
Publicity.

11:30.898 --> 11:32.817
Right now, I think this is the best way--

11:32.900 --> 11:37.238
But this is clearly a breach of contract
and is disrespectful to the artist--

11:37.321 --> 11:39.990
I'm not sure about that.
I already checked the contract

11:40.074 --> 11:41.867
and there doesn't seem to be a problem.

11:42.701 --> 11:43.994
Disrespectful…

11:44.954 --> 11:47.206
You're being unusually emotional.

11:47.289 --> 11:50.251
This could be a great opportunity
for both artists.

11:51.001 --> 11:52.628
So what is the problem?

12:02.972 --> 12:04.515
I'm disappointed in you.

12:04.598 --> 12:08.227
I thought you were more like me.

12:08.310 --> 12:11.480
I guess you don't know how to keep
private matters separate from work.

12:15.526 --> 12:17.403
Let's have a meeting about his later--

12:17.486 --> 12:19.572
You're going to have to apologize.

12:20.573 --> 12:23.826
- Pardon?
- I'm telling you

12:23.909 --> 12:26.662
that you're going to have to
apologize to Go-oh.

12:27.621 --> 12:29.248
- Ms. Kook.
- I'm not being emotional.

12:29.331 --> 12:30.416
I'm being empathetic.

12:31.000 --> 12:34.420
Being good at your job without
empathy isn't something to be proud of.

12:34.503 --> 12:36.630
Empathy is linked to intelligence.

12:36.714 --> 12:40.551
You lacked respect
for the artists and their art, Mr. Jang.

12:42.094 --> 12:46.015
What you need to do is
apologize to him in person.

12:46.724 --> 12:49.894
And it will be up to me
to pick up the pieces as the project lead.

12:49.977 --> 12:52.646
I hope there aren't
any more surprises like this.

12:57.026 --> 13:00.404
I can't believe you thought
I was like you.

13:01.155 --> 13:03.199
It makes me reflect on my past actions.

13:08.245 --> 13:09.371
Should we get going too?

13:09.455 --> 13:11.415
Let's go. It's over.

13:22.593 --> 13:24.512
Ung has always been this way.

13:25.513 --> 13:26.680
Are you okay?

13:28.015 --> 13:29.016
Yes.

13:29.099 --> 13:31.435
He's usually calm and quiet.

13:32.061 --> 13:35.814
But his whole world would shatter
whenever Yeon-su appeared.

13:36.857 --> 13:38.567
The Choi Ung I knew

13:39.443 --> 13:41.779
was always unfaltering.

13:42.738 --> 13:43.989
Over here.

13:44.073 --> 13:45.241
Let's go.

13:45.324 --> 13:46.700
Let's get some rest.

13:46.784 --> 13:48.035
Go in deep.

13:52.206 --> 13:54.917
Hey, stop drawing
and shoot some hoops with us.

13:56.085 --> 13:57.086
Come on.

13:58.462 --> 14:01.340
He had no interest in the world.

14:02.007 --> 14:03.259
Here.

14:05.010 --> 14:07.179
- Look, it's Kook Yeon-su.
- Who?

14:07.263 --> 14:09.765
The girl who entered the school
with the highest grades.

14:09.848 --> 14:12.059
She's pretty but she's stuck-up.

14:21.443 --> 14:23.571
That was until Yeon-su appeared.

14:35.165 --> 14:36.834
I know it may sound weird,

14:36.917 --> 14:43.716
but I always thought Choi Ung was
neither happy nor sad like me.

14:49.471 --> 14:51.140
But everything changed.

14:51.223 --> 14:53.434
I got a girlfriend.

15:00.649 --> 15:01.817
Did you break up again?

15:02.776 --> 15:06.280
When it came to Yeon-su,
even the littlest things would shake him.

15:08.908 --> 15:11.660
Is this the fifth time? The sixth?

15:13.412 --> 15:15.623
Shouldn't you be used to it by now?

15:16.248 --> 15:18.542
Just be sad once every two breakups.

15:27.134 --> 15:30.220
He would become immature
and not be able to control his emotions.

15:36.769 --> 15:37.811
Hey.

15:40.689 --> 15:42.691
Never mind. We'll talk later.

15:57.456 --> 15:58.791
I'm home.

15:59.375 --> 16:02.878
You're here early.
I thought you were going to be late.

16:03.379 --> 16:05.422
Then you should have just gone to bed.

16:05.506 --> 16:06.799
What are you doing outside?

16:07.883 --> 16:10.386
I have to see my granddaughter
come home before I sleep.

16:11.470 --> 16:16.475
Gosh, my granddaughter looks
so pretty wearing that.

16:16.558 --> 16:19.269
Your granddaughter looks pretty
wearing regular clothes too.

16:19.353 --> 16:21.313
Goodness. What were you doing?

16:21.397 --> 16:22.773
Nothing special.

16:24.358 --> 16:27.027
So how was the party or whatever?

16:28.320 --> 16:30.656
Everyone was so relaxed and cool

16:30.739 --> 16:33.784
as if they were taught
how to be like that.

16:43.669 --> 16:45.337
Were you alone all day?

16:45.421 --> 16:48.257
Yes, I guess.

16:49.591 --> 16:52.928
How come your friend
hasn't been visiting these days?

16:54.054 --> 16:55.597
She's probably busy.

16:56.223 --> 16:57.599
Did you two fight?

16:57.683 --> 16:59.560
Of course not.

17:00.144 --> 17:05.816
She kept talking nonsense,
so I just set her straight.

17:05.899 --> 17:06.900
We didn't fight.

17:06.984 --> 17:08.694
So you did fight.

17:08.777 --> 17:12.239
You were harsh on her
and hurt her feelings again, didn't you?

17:12.322 --> 17:14.116
I didn't!

17:14.199 --> 17:17.453
Stop talking nonsense.
Go get washed up and go to sleep.

17:17.536 --> 17:20.247
Gosh, we are so much alike.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.459
Can't you just get along with her?

17:27.004 --> 17:28.839
Go see her tomorrow.

17:28.922 --> 17:31.633
- No thank you.
- Then I'll bring her here.

17:31.717 --> 17:35.554
I told you no.
She probably doesn't want to.

17:37.931 --> 17:40.350
Stop being so stubborn
and apologize to her.

17:58.285 --> 18:00.329
Stop being so stubborn and apologize.

18:01.747 --> 18:02.790
For what?

18:03.916 --> 18:07.294
You should have realized by now
what you've done wrong.

18:08.087 --> 18:10.839
But you didn't call me or come see me

18:12.257 --> 18:13.967
because of your pride.

18:14.843 --> 18:18.388
I know you've been thinking about
what to do all day.

18:20.224 --> 18:21.308
Who? Me?

18:21.934 --> 18:25.479
That's why I came to you first.
I'll give you a chance. Go ahead.

18:58.387 --> 19:00.556
How is it that hard
for you to say you're sorry?

19:03.851 --> 19:05.686
I can't because I haven't done it often.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.688
Then start doing it more often
from now on.

19:08.355 --> 19:10.941
Then everyone will think I'm a pushover.

19:11.024 --> 19:11.984
I don't want to lose.

19:14.278 --> 19:15.904
Then I'll be on my way.

19:22.327 --> 19:23.620
Sorry.

19:25.455 --> 19:26.999
I was wrong.

19:29.918 --> 19:31.587
What? I can't hear you.

19:33.172 --> 19:36.633
I said I'm sorry.

19:42.306 --> 19:45.017
You idiot. It's okay to say that to me.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.562
I'll keep coming back to you.

19:48.645 --> 19:50.647
All you have to do is apologize.

19:52.024 --> 19:53.609
I'm the one who gives in
in the end anyway.

20:04.703 --> 20:06.371
He must be really angry.

20:08.332 --> 20:10.959
He'll probably be bottling it up.

21:17.651 --> 21:19.528
Are you going somewhere?

21:19.611 --> 21:22.489
Oh, there's something
I need to take care of,

21:22.572 --> 21:24.491
so I'm going to go see Ung.

21:24.574 --> 21:26.326
Some things happened yesterday,

21:26.410 --> 21:27.911
so I'm going to go apologize.

21:27.995 --> 21:32.165
It's not like I did something wrong.
It was a small misunderstanding.

21:32.749 --> 21:37.087
It's just that it's something
he'd be upset about.

21:37.170 --> 21:40.507
So I'm going to go talk to him.

21:41.508 --> 21:43.510
I'm sure he's home.

21:43.593 --> 21:44.594
Did you call him?

21:46.013 --> 21:49.391
I did yesterday,
but I think he was asleep.

21:49.474 --> 21:50.851
I'll call him again.

21:55.939 --> 21:58.942
But I swear this wasn't my fault.

21:59.026 --> 22:01.403
He let his imagination run wild
and is blaming me.

22:01.486 --> 22:04.990
Does he really think
I'd do something like that?

22:09.494 --> 22:12.414
Even so, he said that I ruined his life.

22:12.497 --> 22:14.624
It's a bit harsh, don't you think?

22:14.708 --> 22:17.294
How in the world did I ruin his life?

22:19.713 --> 22:22.382
The person you have called cannot…

22:25.427 --> 22:30.223
If so, there's no reason
for me to go him, right?

22:30.307 --> 22:33.935
I can just sort everything out
and call him later, right?

22:34.978 --> 22:36.938
I changed my mind. I'm not going.

22:37.022 --> 22:38.106
Hey!

22:38.648 --> 22:40.358
Yeon-su!

22:42.360 --> 22:44.488
What's strange is that…

22:45.072 --> 22:48.742
It's supposed to be quiet here
since I live alone,

22:48.825 --> 22:53.080
but I find it very awkward right now.

22:53.914 --> 22:55.123
Ung!

22:55.916 --> 22:57.334
Because I'm now used to that.

23:02.464 --> 23:03.799
Hello, Ji-ung.

23:06.176 --> 23:08.804
Ung, I heard what happened yesterday.

23:08.887 --> 23:10.514
It's about time.

23:10.597 --> 23:12.432
How could that happen?

23:12.516 --> 23:15.060
I know. I'm dumbfounded as well.

23:15.143 --> 23:17.521
How could you go to a party without me?

23:17.604 --> 23:19.856
You were invited but didn't take me.

23:19.940 --> 23:23.110
You saw me watch TV all alone yesterday.

23:23.193 --> 23:25.987
How could you go alone,
dressed up like a penguin?

23:26.071 --> 23:27.614
Shut up.

23:27.697 --> 23:31.868
And shouldn't you be
asking me if I'm okay?

23:31.952 --> 23:33.703
- What do you mean?
- What do you think?

23:33.787 --> 23:38.208
- They got Nu-a onboard without me knowing.
- Oh, that? Isn't it okay, though?

23:38.291 --> 23:42.003
When you two have a drawing show
you can take him down a peg.

23:42.087 --> 23:44.881
- And the plagiarism charges will go away.
- What?

23:44.965 --> 23:47.425
Of course, that's just what I think.

23:47.509 --> 23:51.972
I gave them hell.
"How could do us dirty like that?"

23:52.055 --> 23:55.642
"It was a difficult decision
for us to make. This is unacceptable."

23:55.725 --> 23:58.687
I told them in a very cold
and professional way.

23:58.770 --> 23:59.855
I'm impressed.

24:00.730 --> 24:04.401
As you can see,
I'm a very competent manager.

24:06.653 --> 24:08.572
You should be filming me.

24:09.322 --> 24:10.907
Let's just give it more thought.

24:10.991 --> 24:13.326
You are great at what you do.

24:13.410 --> 24:16.413
This is a chance for you
to humiliate him in public.

24:22.043 --> 24:23.336
But Ung.

24:23.837 --> 24:28.091
Maybe you should show them
something more artistic.

24:29.134 --> 24:32.012
- What?
- Come on. Think about it.

24:32.095 --> 24:35.724
If the viewers see this,
they'll think all you do is eat and sleep.

24:35.807 --> 24:39.853
Shouldn't you show them
your professional side?

24:39.936 --> 24:43.899
Hey, I hate being putting on airs
and being fake.

24:44.774 --> 24:47.068
Documentaries are about
showing your natural self.

24:47.152 --> 24:50.614
I hate doing things I wouldn't normally do
just because he's filming.

24:50.697 --> 24:54.826
Don't expect me to be all pretentious.

24:58.413 --> 25:01.791
Whenever I have time,
I come to the museum to enjoy art.

25:01.875 --> 25:04.419
It's important for people like me

25:05.462 --> 25:08.215
to be constantly stimulated and inspired.

25:10.175 --> 25:12.719
I'm sure the video from ten years ago

25:12.802 --> 25:14.512
never showed this side of me.

25:15.263 --> 25:17.057
How do I put this…

25:17.557 --> 25:22.103
The homogenized Korean education system
forces you into conformity.

25:22.187 --> 25:27.234
That was why it was
so hard for me spread my wings.

25:28.568 --> 25:31.738
I can say that this is my true self.

25:33.156 --> 25:34.741
We're done.

25:34.824 --> 25:36.284
Sorry. We ran out of battery.

25:37.619 --> 25:40.789
- You didn't get any of that?
- Yes. I'm going to change the batteries.

25:41.748 --> 25:43.750
Hey. You should be
shooting things like this.

25:43.833 --> 25:47.254
- You only shot useless stuff.
- My camera doesn't want to film you.

25:47.337 --> 25:49.673
- Did it just throw up? Are you okay?
- Do you want to die?

25:49.756 --> 25:52.175
- I'll go get it.
- It's fine. I'll go get it.

25:52.259 --> 25:53.510
You need batteries, right?

25:55.136 --> 25:56.137
I'll be right back.

26:08.525 --> 26:11.653
Of course, this is none of my business.

26:11.736 --> 26:13.238
Has Yeon-su called you?

26:14.990 --> 26:15.991
Why do you ask?

26:16.658 --> 26:17.867
Well, after what happened…

26:17.951 --> 26:20.161
Shouldn't you meet her in person
and talk it out?

26:21.246 --> 26:22.539
I'll take care of it.

26:22.622 --> 26:24.207
I'm sure you will.

26:24.708 --> 26:27.627
But if you're going to do it,
do it in front of the camera.

26:29.504 --> 26:31.798
You're taking everything you can,
aren't you?

26:32.507 --> 26:33.425
Forget it.

26:43.810 --> 26:45.270
I shouldn't have butted in.

26:45.353 --> 26:47.230
You're avoiding her because you're sorry.

26:49.232 --> 26:51.484
- What?
- You weren't that bothered

26:51.568 --> 26:53.028
by what happened yesterday.

26:53.653 --> 26:56.656
You're not the kind of person
who gets upset over things like that.

26:58.033 --> 26:58.908
What do you mean?

26:58.992 --> 27:01.578
You were mad at her,
and it had nothing to do with work.

27:02.245 --> 27:06.082
You also know that Yeon-su
wouldn't have done that on purpose.

27:07.959 --> 27:10.712
You were taking it out on her
for what happened in the past.

27:12.505 --> 27:14.507
I didn't have to say that.

27:14.591 --> 27:16.134
I can tell…

27:18.178 --> 27:19.888
you still have feelings for her.

27:22.557 --> 27:24.476
What did I expect him to tell me?

27:29.147 --> 27:31.191
Why are so interested in us
all of a sudden?

27:32.400 --> 27:33.985
It's not because of the shoot.

27:35.445 --> 27:37.197
I don't think this is out of the blue.

27:38.323 --> 27:39.282
What do you know?

27:40.450 --> 27:42.243
What don't I know?

27:44.621 --> 27:46.748
What was it that I wanted to check?

27:54.089 --> 27:56.007
Yes!

27:57.092 --> 27:58.802
This is perfect.

27:58.885 --> 28:02.305
There's a group reservation today,
so there was a lot to prepare.

28:02.389 --> 28:05.558
I told you to hire someone.
How are you going to do this by yourself?

28:05.642 --> 28:07.560
And who's going to pay them?

28:07.644 --> 28:11.231
So stop sitting around and help me!
I heard it's your day off.

28:11.314 --> 28:13.858
Do you have to make me work on my day off?

28:13.942 --> 28:16.152
Plus, I'm shooting a documentary.

28:18.321 --> 28:20.990
Don't you want to film her working?

28:21.074 --> 28:22.909
An everyday moment.

28:22.992 --> 28:25.286
You're going to
keep filming her here, right?

28:25.370 --> 28:26.329
Don't mind us.

28:26.413 --> 28:28.415
What do you know?

28:29.082 --> 28:30.125
What is this anyway?

28:37.048 --> 28:38.133
My gosh.

28:39.300 --> 28:40.135
Octopuses?

28:40.218 --> 28:42.720
They were delivered from
Mokpo this morning.

28:43.304 --> 28:46.516
I'll put aside a plate for you.
What do you say?

28:49.185 --> 28:52.689
- What do you need me to do?
- I've known Yeon-su for ten years.

28:52.772 --> 28:54.649
We met when we were in college.

28:54.733 --> 28:57.819
As you all know,
she can be a bit of a **tch.

28:57.902 --> 29:00.113
So we became friends after a huge fight.

29:00.196 --> 29:02.741
I get along well with crazy **tches.

29:02.824 --> 29:04.951
Excuse me. Why are you shooting her?

29:05.034 --> 29:07.579
I was a big fan of that video.

29:07.662 --> 29:09.205
I wrote a lot of comments.

29:09.289 --> 29:11.791
My handle is "I'm Writer Lee."

29:11.875 --> 29:15.211
- I used to write scripts for TV shows.
- You're supposed to be filming me.

29:15.295 --> 29:17.922
Have you heard of a show called
Omniscient Psychopath's View?

29:18.006 --> 29:19.632
I was the one who wrote it.

29:19.716 --> 29:23.386
And I opened this little bar
using the money I made.

29:23.470 --> 29:25.722
I actually used to have a partner.

29:25.805 --> 29:28.224
He was my then-boyfriend.

29:28.308 --> 29:30.435
They never asked to hear your life story.

29:30.518 --> 29:34.022
On the day when I deposited the premium,
I caught that asshole cheating on me.

29:34.105 --> 29:36.733
That idiot. I caught him red-handed.

29:36.816 --> 29:38.568
So I cut him off

29:38.651 --> 29:40.987
and was barely able to
open the bar by myself.

29:41.070 --> 29:43.531
No one wants to know.

29:43.615 --> 29:45.784
Do you think that asshole is
watching right now?

29:46.618 --> 29:48.828
Jin-seob, are you watching?

29:48.912 --> 29:51.623
A group of ten people
made a reservation today.

29:51.706 --> 29:54.375
I'm doing just fine
and I hope you're doing fine too.

29:54.459 --> 29:57.045
So do you also know Choi Ung?

29:58.004 --> 30:00.006
Of course. I know him very well.

30:00.089 --> 30:01.883
- When they were in college--
- Look here.

30:01.966 --> 30:04.677
There are many onions here.
Is this a Chinese restaurant?

30:04.761 --> 30:06.805
If you want to know anything, ask away.

30:06.888 --> 30:09.390
I'll even do an interview
if you film my bar properly.

30:09.974 --> 30:11.935
- Hey. Here's the battery.
- Thanks.

30:13.061 --> 30:14.145
Where's Ung?

30:15.855 --> 30:18.900
- Something came up and he had to go.
- What is it?

30:18.983 --> 30:21.820
Is it something I don't know about?
Wait. He just left me here?

30:21.903 --> 30:23.530
Can't you see he left me here too?

30:23.613 --> 30:26.533
Gosh. He sure is reckless these days.

30:26.616 --> 30:29.828
This won't do. As his manager,
I'll give him a piece of my mind.

30:30.662 --> 30:31.913
Where are you going?

30:31.996 --> 30:33.873
I… Hold on.

30:39.420 --> 30:41.172
Yes. What is it?

30:43.091 --> 30:45.510
Now? Today?

30:46.845 --> 30:49.013
You can't give me an hour's notice.

30:50.640 --> 30:52.559
Just send the assistant director.

30:52.642 --> 30:54.352
No, not Chae-ran.

30:57.146 --> 30:58.648
Okay. I'll go.

30:58.731 --> 31:01.234
The camera crew is coming too, right?

31:02.193 --> 31:03.027
Okay.

31:04.362 --> 31:05.697
Did something come up?

31:05.780 --> 31:07.991
- Yes. I have to go.
- Wait…

31:10.076 --> 31:14.330
I don't know what it is,
but can you drop me off on your way there?

31:15.456 --> 31:19.002
I told you about the documentary, right?
He's the producer.

31:19.085 --> 31:21.004
Hello. Give it to her.

31:24.674 --> 31:27.844
We're shooting a special video
for the 700th episode special.

31:27.927 --> 31:29.762
You just have to say congratulations

31:29.846 --> 31:33.266
and a simple greeting to the viewers.

31:33.349 --> 31:34.934
Did the previous producer quit?

31:35.018 --> 31:37.103
I'm just filling in for him today.

31:37.687 --> 31:38.688
I see.

31:38.771 --> 31:42.525
We're all set, so we'll start shooting
as soon as you're ready to go.

31:43.484 --> 31:44.777
Excuse me.

31:46.279 --> 31:47.280
Haven't we met before?

31:49.949 --> 31:51.910
- Pardon?
- Don't you know me?

31:53.369 --> 31:57.874
- I'm sure everyone knows who you are.
- No. When I filmed this four years ago,

31:57.957 --> 32:00.335
weren't you the assistant director?

32:00.919 --> 32:02.462
Yes. That's right.

32:02.545 --> 32:06.591
I knew it.
How come you pretended not to know me?

32:06.674 --> 32:08.593
I wasn't sure if you remembered me.

32:09.552 --> 32:12.680
- Well, I tend to remember these things.
- Thank you for remembering.

32:13.514 --> 32:17.101
I was very young,
so I was very nervous back then.

32:17.185 --> 32:19.729
But seeing you acting nervous
in the corner there,

32:19.812 --> 32:21.773
actually comforted me.

32:21.856 --> 32:25.360
You can just talk about the video
naturally like you did just now.

32:25.443 --> 32:28.112
Honestly, I don't remember
much from back then.

32:28.196 --> 32:31.783
My schedule was pretty packed
and a lot of cameras were pointed at me.

32:31.866 --> 32:34.285
And I didn't even know
which companies they were from.

32:34.369 --> 32:38.498
Oh, I remember! It was when
they were shooting me meditate.

32:38.581 --> 32:41.042
You were in the corner with
a kettle and you dozed off.

32:41.125 --> 32:43.378
You dropped it
and were scolded because of that.

32:43.461 --> 32:45.755
I was actually half-asleep
when I was meditating.

32:45.838 --> 32:48.257
I was tired, so I lied I was meditating.

32:49.425 --> 32:51.844
The sound of that kettle dropping
woke me up.

32:51.928 --> 32:52.762
I see.

32:53.513 --> 32:55.139
Shall we talk about something else?

32:55.723 --> 32:57.767
You seem very different from then.

33:00.019 --> 33:02.230
What program are you filming these days?

33:02.313 --> 33:06.275
- It seems like you're in charge now.
- I'm doing a special show.

33:06.359 --> 33:09.404
Special? What is it about?

33:12.115 --> 33:14.909
Here's a plate of sliced raw octopus
that looks just like you.

33:16.869 --> 33:20.540
Now that I think about it,
I don't think this covers my labor costs.

33:21.582 --> 33:22.792
Eat up.

33:23.626 --> 33:25.962
- Do you want a bottle of soju?
- Yes.

33:28.506 --> 33:30.591
Coming right up.

33:30.675 --> 33:32.176
Yes, this is Leezakaya.

33:32.760 --> 33:34.637
Yes. 6:30 p.m., ten people.

33:34.721 --> 33:36.139
What name are you under?

33:36.889 --> 33:39.017
Yes. You want to cancel?

33:40.393 --> 33:41.436
I see.

33:42.437 --> 33:43.688
I guess it can't be helped.

33:44.397 --> 33:45.231
Okay.

33:47.066 --> 33:50.111
I'll pay for this.

33:53.239 --> 33:56.826
This pub is going down in flames!

33:57.702 --> 34:00.204
Why would they order octopus
if they're going to cancel?

34:00.288 --> 34:04.125
Excuse me, can you shoot this

34:04.208 --> 34:07.295
and send it to one of those
current affairs shows?

34:07.378 --> 34:09.464
Gosh, this is so stressful.

34:11.090 --> 34:13.384
What am I supposed to do
with the octopuses?

34:14.510 --> 34:17.388
Let's try to attract customers with them.

34:17.472 --> 34:19.432
When they come, just serve octopus.

34:21.142 --> 34:23.144
Have you ever seen customers here?

34:24.020 --> 34:26.731
Well, maybe like one or two…

34:30.276 --> 34:31.527
What can I do?

34:32.320 --> 34:33.362
Eat up.

34:34.947 --> 34:37.158
You two should come and join us.

34:42.246 --> 34:43.790
Is there anyone you can call over?

34:43.873 --> 34:45.583
Me? What do you think?

34:45.666 --> 34:47.460
Why am I your only friend?

34:47.543 --> 34:48.419
What about you?

34:48.503 --> 34:51.047
I have a lot of exes.

34:51.130 --> 34:53.132
But you only have one ex-boyfriend.

34:54.675 --> 34:55.927
Excuse me.

34:57.553 --> 34:58.971
I know someone we can call.

35:04.102 --> 35:06.062
SBC CURRENT AFFAIRS AND CULTURE
PRODUCER JUNG CHAE-RAN

35:08.648 --> 35:10.775
Hey. How's it going over there?

35:11.901 --> 35:12.819
Yes.

35:12.902 --> 35:14.362
DON'T WALK, RUN
RUNNING MAN

35:16.322 --> 35:18.282
I see. That's great.

35:18.366 --> 35:20.326
I'll be there once we're done here.

35:20.409 --> 35:21.410
Okay.

35:23.996 --> 35:25.706
You're the intern, right?

35:25.790 --> 35:27.834
Yes, I'm Im Tae-hun.

35:27.917 --> 35:30.002
Go home and get some rest.
I'll wrap it up here.

35:30.086 --> 35:32.255
- No, wait--
- I won't say it again. Go home.

35:34.882 --> 35:36.134
Thank you, sir!

35:41.347 --> 35:43.432
Gosh, you're amazing.

35:43.516 --> 35:44.851
You didn't have to do that.

35:44.934 --> 35:48.354
When they come,
I will only charge them for the octopus.

35:48.437 --> 35:49.814
Alcohol will be on the house.

35:49.897 --> 35:52.066
Come here and have a drink.

35:52.150 --> 35:54.861
Come to think of it,
we've never had a meal together.

35:54.944 --> 35:57.697
- Thanks, but I'm okay.
- Just turn off the camera and come.

35:57.780 --> 36:00.616
Here. Let's see.

36:00.700 --> 36:02.034
Do you like octopuses?

36:02.535 --> 36:04.996
- Gosh.
- That little…

36:05.079 --> 36:08.958
Why would you try to feed
a grown-up and make a mess?

36:09.041 --> 36:10.209
Welcome--

36:11.627 --> 36:12.628
Wait.

36:13.337 --> 36:14.422
What?

36:15.131 --> 36:16.924
It's been a while.

36:22.680 --> 36:26.392
Meeting like this out of the blue
wasn't part of the plan.

36:29.103 --> 36:32.023
What are you doing here?

36:32.106 --> 36:33.983
I heard we're shooting something here.

36:35.276 --> 36:37.403
I came because
I heard there will be octopus.

36:43.159 --> 36:44.827
I first met Ung

36:44.911 --> 36:47.455
when I was working part-time
at his father's shop.

36:47.538 --> 36:51.250
There was this unemployed bum
who sat around doing nothing.

36:51.334 --> 36:54.754
He turned out to be their son.

36:54.837 --> 36:57.298
So I approached him--

36:57.381 --> 36:58.883
I can hear you.

36:58.966 --> 37:01.928
I noticed that he often doodled
on small pieces of paper.

37:02.011 --> 37:05.139
And my animalistic instinct
told me that this was it.

37:05.223 --> 37:07.433
I saw his potential and knew he'd succeed.

37:07.516 --> 37:10.937
So that's when I became his manager.

37:11.938 --> 37:14.899
I'm actually known to be very diligent.

37:15.942 --> 37:17.902
I don't think anyone asked.

37:17.985 --> 37:20.613
Anyway, since I've known him the longest,

37:20.696 --> 37:22.615
you can ask me anything you want.

37:22.698 --> 37:25.826
What do you want to know?
His job? His past relationships?

37:25.910 --> 37:27.245
Hold on.

37:27.870 --> 37:29.372
Haven't we met before?

37:31.207 --> 37:33.709
- That's not going to work on me.
- I'm sorry.

37:33.793 --> 37:35.086
Enjoy.

37:35.169 --> 37:36.754
Let me use the bathroom for a bit.

37:53.604 --> 37:56.732
I should apologize to him first, right?

37:57.316 --> 37:58.776
Right.

37:58.859 --> 38:02.321
Since I'm more mature,
I should talk to him.

38:03.823 --> 38:05.741
- Ung, about yesterday--
- I'm sorry.

38:06.242 --> 38:09.287
What I said yesterday was just nonsense.
Just forget what I said.

38:10.288 --> 38:12.915
I was upset,
so words just came flying out of my mouth.

38:14.792 --> 38:15.793
I see.

38:16.919 --> 38:19.130
Still, I was in the wrong.

38:19.213 --> 38:21.215
- I'm sorry--
- I know it wasn't your fault.

38:21.299 --> 38:22.466
It's okay.

38:27.179 --> 38:28.014
Okay.

38:30.391 --> 38:33.686
Both my team and the Soen Shop

38:33.769 --> 38:35.688
will make a formal apology.

38:35.771 --> 38:39.025
- And I'll change it back--
- I'll do it.

38:40.443 --> 38:42.862
- What?
- I'll work with Nu-a.

38:45.573 --> 38:47.366
What? Why?

38:48.451 --> 38:50.161
There's no reason for me not to.

38:51.287 --> 38:52.872
That's true, but…

38:53.622 --> 38:56.250
And you don't have to apologize.
I already went to see him.

38:57.335 --> 38:58.794
- Who?
- Mr. Jang.

38:59.920 --> 39:02.798
- You went to see him? When?
- He called me earlier.

39:02.882 --> 39:06.510
What did he say to you? Did he apologize?

39:06.594 --> 39:09.930
And what did you tell him?
Did you just brush it off again?

39:10.014 --> 39:12.808
You should tell him if you were offended
and have him apologize--

39:12.892 --> 39:13.768
I'll…

39:16.228 --> 39:17.438
take care of it.

39:22.777 --> 39:23.861
But…

39:24.737 --> 39:28.282
why does Ung seem like a stranger today?

39:31.243 --> 39:32.328
Okay.

39:33.204 --> 39:34.330
Got it.

39:35.122 --> 39:39.085
Anyway, we only have
a week until the opening,

39:39.168 --> 39:41.128
so I'll make sure to be ready for it.

39:42.296 --> 39:44.340
I'm sorry for being so childish.

39:44.423 --> 39:48.052
Of course, things are now going
the way they're supposed to.

39:48.135 --> 39:49.678
And the documentary…

39:50.679 --> 39:54.183
I agreed to shoot for a month,
so I'll do my best.

39:55.684 --> 39:57.353
Let's end this smoothly.

39:58.479 --> 40:00.940
What is this I'm feeling?

40:05.694 --> 40:08.697
Okay. Let's do that.

40:14.078 --> 40:17.498
Why do I feel like
something is out of place?

40:32.888 --> 40:33.764
What are you doing?

40:36.350 --> 40:38.686
At least pretend to be surprised.
You're so boring.

40:40.563 --> 40:42.523
What are you doing here on a weekend?

40:42.606 --> 40:46.360
Did you get a haircut? What about
your blind date? Were you turned down?

40:46.986 --> 40:49.155
- She said my hair looks like a wig.
- I see.

40:49.238 --> 40:50.990
What are you doing here at this hour?

40:51.073 --> 40:53.117
I'm making backups
of what we filmed today.

40:54.493 --> 40:58.038
I heard Tae-jin made you fill in for him.

40:58.122 --> 41:01.041
- Why didn't he make Chae-ran do it?
- She's out shooting.

41:01.625 --> 41:05.421
And I asked for an additional
team member, not an intern.

41:05.504 --> 41:07.756
So you sent him back.

41:07.840 --> 41:10.509
Send him back to me.
Don't make him go from team to team.

41:10.593 --> 41:11.969
Just have him work on my team.

41:12.052 --> 41:15.848
Gosh, you are more
kindhearted than you look.

41:15.931 --> 41:17.141
Come here, you.

41:19.727 --> 41:21.145
How's the shoot going?

41:21.812 --> 41:25.149
I haven't heard from you in a while.
Why aren't you sharing anything?

41:25.232 --> 41:27.359
Things are neither good nor bad.

41:28.110 --> 41:30.070
Gosh, I'm curious
to see what they're like.

41:30.154 --> 41:32.114
Maybe I should go visit the shoot.

41:32.990 --> 41:35.326
What about you? Are you having fun?

41:37.036 --> 41:38.245
Well…

41:39.413 --> 41:41.332
Maybe I shouldn't have taken the job.

41:42.208 --> 41:44.084
Hey, is that fun?

41:44.168 --> 41:45.377
What do you mean?

41:45.461 --> 41:47.379
Shooting someone with a camera.

41:48.422 --> 41:51.717
Oh, this? Of course, it's fun.

41:51.800 --> 41:55.054
Looking into other people's lives is fun.

41:55.137 --> 41:59.517
You end up meeting
all kinds of people in the world

42:00.226 --> 42:03.479
and end up feeling grateful
for your insipid life.

42:04.980 --> 42:06.232
Why do you ask?

42:06.315 --> 42:09.401
Does it really make you feel grateful
for your insipid life?

42:13.155 --> 42:14.156
What is it?

42:14.240 --> 42:17.117
It's not boring,
so stop looking at me like that.

42:17.201 --> 42:18.744
This is just how I look.

42:18.827 --> 42:21.705
And just give it time. It'll become fun.

42:21.789 --> 42:24.708
You'll realize why I gave you this job.

42:24.792 --> 42:26.377
Because I was available?

42:26.460 --> 42:27.962
Gosh, don't talk like that.

42:28.045 --> 42:31.382
I can't believe you don't see
how thoughtful I am.

42:31.465 --> 42:34.176
Find out why I put you
in charge of this. That's your homework.

42:34.260 --> 42:35.427
I'm off.

42:37.429 --> 42:38.847
Have you been drinking?

42:44.770 --> 42:45.854
Here.

42:46.397 --> 42:47.690
It's on the house.

42:48.232 --> 42:50.651
It's fresh clams.
I made a stew out of them.

42:50.734 --> 42:53.779
It's on the house
since I haven't seen you in a long time.

42:53.862 --> 42:55.823
You're looking good. How long has it been?

42:56.490 --> 42:58.075
After you two broke--

42:59.410 --> 43:03.247
I mean, we haven't seen each other
since our graduation.

43:03.330 --> 43:04.540
It's been a while, right?

43:04.623 --> 43:06.750
You're right. It has been a while.

43:06.834 --> 43:09.253
I heard you're quite successful
as an illustrator.

43:09.336 --> 43:11.422
No, he's doing great!

43:11.505 --> 43:14.300
He's practically a star. Am I right?

43:14.383 --> 43:17.761
You used to draw, right?
Is that what you do these days?

43:17.845 --> 43:20.264
He's killing it out there
with his drawings.

43:20.347 --> 43:23.601
Even Yeon-su came to ask him
to work with him.

43:23.684 --> 43:24.727
Need I say more?

43:24.810 --> 43:27.855
You can never tell
what's going to happen in life.

43:27.938 --> 43:31.233
Who would have known
that the tables would turn like that

43:31.317 --> 43:32.610
after their breakup--

43:38.907 --> 43:41.035
- I'm going to go get some air.
- Let's go.

43:41.118 --> 43:43.162
- Do you smoke?
- No, but I'm going outside.

43:43.245 --> 43:44.788
Me neither, but I'm going anyway.

43:45.789 --> 43:47.833
- This way.
- Thank you.

43:51.378 --> 43:54.298
Gosh, they messed everything up.

44:00.346 --> 44:03.515
Why does he keep acting like this?

44:04.892 --> 44:06.393
What else did you ask?

44:06.477 --> 44:09.521
Is he still mad? Or…

44:09.605 --> 44:14.276
It's been ten years
since you two met on video.

44:14.360 --> 44:15.861
How do you feel?

44:16.528 --> 44:19.865
It was a long time ago,
so my memory was a little hazy,

44:20.449 --> 44:23.869
but it was
surprisingly nice to see her again.

44:23.952 --> 44:26.955
If you saw the video,
you know we don't get along too well.

44:31.085 --> 44:33.212
Could he really be okay?

44:34.171 --> 44:35.172
Ms. Kook?

44:36.715 --> 44:37.800
Ms. Kook.

44:38.634 --> 44:40.135
- Yes?
- How do you feel?

44:40.803 --> 44:41.804
Well…

44:42.888 --> 44:44.890
It was pretty much the same for me.

44:44.973 --> 44:47.893
I was happy and surprised to see him.

45:21.885 --> 45:23.762
- You're here.
- Hello.

45:24.430 --> 45:28.392
Go-oh sent us a proposal this morning
regarding the collaboration.

45:28.475 --> 45:30.936
- It's on our drive, so please take a look.
- Sure.

45:31.019 --> 45:32.771
- We haven't heard from Nu-a yet.
- Okay.

45:32.855 --> 45:34.940
We'll discuss it
after I take a look at it.

45:35.023 --> 45:36.275
- Okay.
- Okay.

45:36.358 --> 45:37.818
100 HOURS OF WORK
5 HOURS OF LIVE DRAWING

45:38.861 --> 45:39.987
A hundred hours?

45:40.487 --> 45:43.699
Is he really going to work for
one hundred hours?

45:43.782 --> 45:44.950
I know, right?

45:45.033 --> 45:47.995
I think he's going to show us
his work process for the first time.

45:48.078 --> 45:51.665
He says he's going to record
his entire work process.

45:51.748 --> 45:54.960
Can he do that in five days? Oh my.

45:55.043 --> 45:57.087
He's going to work for five days

45:57.171 --> 46:00.132
and draw the rest live
on the day of the opening.

46:00.215 --> 46:02.384
How is that even possible?

46:03.093 --> 46:05.304
So aside from when he eats and sleeps,

46:05.387 --> 46:07.848
he's going to draw for 19 hours a day?

46:07.931 --> 46:08.974
Something like that.

46:10.267 --> 46:12.811
He's a far greater artist than I thought.

46:19.067 --> 46:21.695
Make sure everything is set up.

46:21.778 --> 46:25.199
Make sure to check everything
thoroughly at the scene.

46:25.282 --> 46:27.117
And as for Myeong-ho, I want you to…

46:30.370 --> 46:33.123
The event will consist of
the opening ceremony, the opening,

46:33.207 --> 46:35.501
the live drawing show, and the closing.

46:35.584 --> 46:38.128
Next, I'll guide you through the details.

46:38.212 --> 46:42.049
After the cake cutting ceremony,
we'll take a group photo.

46:43.550 --> 46:45.260
Yes, it's done.

46:45.344 --> 46:47.429
Put that there.

46:47.513 --> 46:51.517
We'll put one camera on top
and one over here.

46:51.600 --> 46:52.893
Yes.

46:59.358 --> 47:01.235
Let me call you back.

47:32.599 --> 47:36.395
As you can see, it says gamjatang.

47:36.478 --> 47:39.273
We weren't really trying to
run a business when we started it.

47:39.356 --> 47:41.233
Let's have gamjatang for dinner.

47:41.316 --> 47:43.652
It's something our family used to enjoy--

47:43.735 --> 47:46.113
- Let's go to the chicken feet restaurant.
- Chicken feet?

47:46.196 --> 47:48.907
- And the seafood soup.
- He's so excited.

47:54.037 --> 47:55.414
Welcome.

47:55.497 --> 47:57.499
- A table for two, please.
- Did you just get off work?

47:57.583 --> 47:59.084
- Yes.
- Let me know once you decide.

47:59.167 --> 48:00.294
Okay.

48:00.377 --> 48:02.087
Thank you. Come again.

48:02.170 --> 48:03.672
- Excuse me.
- Coming!

50:00.872 --> 50:01.915
I'm home.

50:01.998 --> 50:03.417
You must be tired.

50:33.989 --> 50:37.033
CHOI UNG

50:45.208 --> 50:48.712
- Make sure they get more exposure.
- Sure.

50:48.795 --> 50:51.840
What do you think about this space?

50:51.923 --> 50:54.593
I'll make sure
this entire space is in the shot.

50:54.676 --> 50:56.011
All right. Moving on.

51:23.830 --> 51:24.664
Ms. Kook.

51:27.667 --> 51:28.752
Ms. Kook.

51:29.795 --> 51:31.254
Hi, Ye-in.

51:31.338 --> 51:33.673
You should go home.
You have a big day tomorrow.

51:33.757 --> 51:36.676
You should go get some rest too.
Good work today.

51:38.678 --> 51:42.766
How much do you think Go-oh did so far?

51:43.642 --> 51:44.851
Do you think he succeeded?

51:46.228 --> 51:49.064
I'm sure he did.

51:50.232 --> 51:53.401
I bet he didn't even have time
to sleep or eat.

51:54.736 --> 51:56.363
Being an artist must be difficult.

51:57.030 --> 51:58.907
I'll get going then.

52:14.965 --> 52:16.341
GU EUN-HO

52:18.677 --> 52:21.930
The phone you are calling
is currently turned off.

52:22.013 --> 52:24.641
Your call will be directed
to voicemail after the tone.

52:26.476 --> 52:28.186
KIM JI-UNG

52:31.439 --> 52:32.858
What's up?

52:32.941 --> 52:34.401
Ji-ung.

52:35.902 --> 52:38.864
How's Ung? Is he doing okay?

52:38.947 --> 52:41.700
Yes. He was doing fine
the last time I saw him.

52:42.367 --> 52:44.286
I see.

52:44.369 --> 52:46.496
If you're worried, go ahead and call him.

52:46.580 --> 52:47.873
No, it's fine.

52:49.207 --> 52:51.877
Eun-ho is with Ung, right?

52:51.960 --> 52:54.129
No, Eun-ho left with me.

52:54.713 --> 52:56.631
He said he wanted to finish up by himself.

52:56.715 --> 52:58.049
Will he be okay alone?

52:58.133 --> 52:59.175
He won't die.

52:59.259 --> 53:02.178
I guess you don't know.
He's like that when he works.

53:02.971 --> 53:03.972
I see.

53:05.849 --> 53:07.100
Okay.

53:07.183 --> 53:09.519
You're coming tomorrow, right?

53:10.854 --> 53:13.064
Okay. See you tomorrow.

54:07.744 --> 54:08.578
GO-OH'S 100 HOURS

54:08.662 --> 54:09.663
EVENT OUTLINE

54:20.382 --> 54:24.094
It won't be weird to call him
since it will be for tomorrow's event.

54:24.177 --> 54:26.096
I'll just see if he's still alive.

54:30.558 --> 54:34.104
He's super sensitive
so he might cause a scene.

54:35.063 --> 54:40.777
Can't he just call me from time to time
to report on his progress?

54:41.444 --> 54:42.821
How frustrating.

54:45.532 --> 54:46.700
Why do I care?

54:48.284 --> 54:49.661
I'm not going to care anymore.

55:00.338 --> 55:03.591
So why am I even here?

55:10.223 --> 55:11.391
No.

55:11.474 --> 55:15.854
I should check up on the artist
since it's important for tomorrow's event.

55:15.937 --> 55:17.689
This is totally acceptable.

55:22.235 --> 55:24.154
Even if the artist wasn't Ung,

55:24.237 --> 55:26.489
I would have done the same thing.

55:26.573 --> 55:29.826
I would have
cared for them even more, right?

55:29.909 --> 55:32.829
It's just purely business.

56:17.499 --> 56:20.460
I rang the bell, but you didn't answer
so I called you.

56:25.298 --> 56:27.342
I didn't come to interrupt.

56:27.425 --> 56:30.929
I wanted to check how it was going
for the event tomorrow, since you…

56:31.012 --> 56:34.849
I mean, checking up on the artist
is also a part of my job.

56:35.517 --> 56:37.519
I came because I was told to.

56:41.189 --> 56:45.360
This is jujube tea. I know you have
a hard time falling asleep…

56:45.443 --> 56:47.487
I mean, they told me to give it to you.

56:48.696 --> 56:50.198
Have some tea and get some sleep.

56:51.908 --> 56:53.118
It was 95 hours.

56:54.786 --> 56:55.912
What?

56:57.455 --> 56:59.249
I just finished working for 95 hours.

57:01.126 --> 57:03.336
I'll draw the rest
in front of the audience tomorrow.

57:04.671 --> 57:06.089
Really?

57:06.172 --> 57:08.299
Did you really manage to do it?

57:08.925 --> 57:10.802
You really are amazing--

57:14.639 --> 57:17.851
Anyway, drink this and get some sleep.

57:24.524 --> 57:27.444
That wasn't so bad, right?

57:28.319 --> 57:29.612
I'm going to go now.

57:30.280 --> 57:32.657
I was very professional.

57:38.246 --> 57:39.330
But…

57:45.920 --> 57:47.130
Do you want to sleep over?

58:07.567 --> 58:14.574
EPILOGUE

58:16.868 --> 58:18.077
I'll do it.

58:18.661 --> 58:21.039
I don't care if I do it with Nu-a
or anyone else.

58:23.750 --> 58:26.211
You're wiser than I thought.

58:27.295 --> 58:28.963
Then we'll just proceed as planned.

58:30.965 --> 58:33.176
I'm sorry for what happened that day.

58:34.385 --> 58:38.139
Well, I was on edge that day.

58:38.765 --> 58:40.266
I'd like to apologize as well.

58:40.350 --> 58:42.894
You were upset at Ms. Kook, not me.

58:52.445 --> 58:53.530
Well…

58:54.656 --> 58:56.324
Can I ask you a personal question?

58:57.325 --> 58:59.118
I can't say that I like it,

58:59.202 --> 59:01.412
but since it's you who's asking, sure.

59:08.920 --> 59:10.004
It's nothing.

59:15.385 --> 59:17.470
You're very easy to read.

59:19.973 --> 59:22.308
When you were looking at Ms. Kook,

59:23.017 --> 59:25.436
it didn't seem like you were over her.

59:26.854 --> 59:28.606
What are you…

59:28.690 --> 59:30.441
I think everyone knows except you.

59:31.192 --> 59:34.320
As long as you don't ruin the project
because of your personal feelings,

59:34.404 --> 59:36.197
I don't really care.

59:36.281 --> 59:39.534
And of course, Ms. Kook assured me
that will never happen.

59:41.369 --> 59:42.704
She did?

59:43.288 --> 59:45.373
As for my answer to your question…

59:48.376 --> 59:51.838
Ms. Kook is very talented.

59:53.840 --> 59:55.383
And that's why I like her.

59:57.927 --> 01:00:00.305
As a business partner, of course.

01:00:00.805 --> 01:00:02.348
It seems it's someone else

01:00:03.016 --> 01:00:06.060
that you should be worried about, not me.

01:00:06.853 --> 01:00:10.398
You're coming tomorrow, right?
See you tomorrow.

01:00:10.481 --> 01:00:11.733
Okay.

01:00:35.757 --> 01:00:42.764
A SECRET THAT CAN'T BE TOLD

01:01:04.118 --> 01:01:07.038
What should I say
if he brings up last night?

01:01:07.872 --> 01:01:11.209
I think I finally appreciate Yeon-su
for who she is.

01:01:11.292 --> 01:01:14.379
Another artist will be
drawing in the next room.

01:01:14.462 --> 01:01:16.089
You'll be too captivated to go there.

01:01:16.172 --> 01:01:19.676
I saw Ung's eyes as he was drawing today.

01:01:19.759 --> 01:01:22.011
They seemed so soulful.

01:01:22.095 --> 01:01:23.805
This is a side of you I haven't seen.

01:01:24.389 --> 01:01:26.849
Do you still like Ung?

01:01:27.392 --> 01:01:32.397
Subtitle translation by: Ju-young Park
